              "id": "modelling_plan",
              "name": "Modelling plan (for Blender / engine agents)",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "RUG — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)\nMetres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a room (space): origin at the room centroid, X/Y in plan, fit inside the room outline.\n\nWHAT IT IS\nplain ivory low-pile area rug, soft tonal abrash, calm minimal bedroom\n\nGEOMETRY\nModel the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:\n- Length: {length}\n- Width: {width}\n- Pile height: {height}\n- Shape: {shape} (one of: Rectangular / Runner / Round)\n- Carved pattern leaves (0 = plain rug): {leaves}\n- Leaf length (largest): {leafLength}\n- Leaf width (largest): {leafWidth}\n- Carved relief of the pattern: {relief}\n- Share of tan leaves (rest sage): {tanShare}\n- Pattern seed: {seed}\n- Border band on the long sides: {showBorder}\n- Border width: {borderWidth}\n- Fringe on the short ends (0 = none): {fringeLength}\n- Rotation (deg): {rotation}\n- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)\n- Margin from host: {margin}\n- Flip side: {flipSide}\nKeep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.\n\nMATERIALS\n- Base colour: {baseColor}\n- Roughness: {roughness}\nPrincipled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.\n\nLIGHTS\nNone. This object does not emit light.\n\nCHECKS (measure after building)\n- Length = {length}\n- Width = {width}\n- Pile height = {height}\n- Leaf length (largest) = {leafLength}\n- Leaf width (largest) = {leafWidth}\n- Border width = {borderWidth}\n- Fringe on the short ends (0 = none) = {fringeLength}\n- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.",
